<title>BELGIUM: Belgian Koramic 1996 profit rises sharply.</title>
<headline>Belgian Koramic 1996 profit rises sharply.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Twelve months to December 31, 1996 (in billions of Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net current profit per share (francs) *  115   vs  148</p>
<p>    Net dividend (francs)  *		     32.5  vs  31.0</p>
<p>    Group net profit				1.221  vs  0.783</p>
<p>    Cons current profit			   1.283  vs  0.845</p>
<p>NOTE - Koramic Building Products NV is a Belgian building materials group. * During 1996 it acquired 25 percent of Austria's Wienerberger Baustoffindustrie. As part of this operation it increased its number of shares to 11,304,927 from 5,699,483.  </p>
<p>    Sales/turnover				 30.484  vs  7.362</p>
<p>    EBDIT -1					  6.114  vs  2.514</p>
<p>    EBIT  -2					  3.452  vs  1.647</p>
<p>    Cons net profit				 1.828  vs  0.783</p>
<p>    Cons current cash flow			3.937  vs  1.645</p>
<p>NOTE 1: Earnings Before Depreciation, Interest and Taxation</p>
<p>NOTE 2: Earnings Before Interest and Taxation</p>
<p>-- Nick Antonovics, Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6817, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
